    "reviewer": "codex-primary-controller",
    "classification": "Compared both versions of UNSD and HS 2022 chapter 26. The June 2025 leaf names iron/steel scalings and nearby 39320, 39340 and 39350 differ in source and physical identity. The October workbook CPC3 row 1910 includes HS 2618 and 2619. The hot-rolling scaling belongs to 2619. Selecting one source, physical recovery route and first sinter feed release supports narrower.",
    "primary_evidence": "Algoma Steel SDS §§1,3 describes reheating/rolling, mixed iron oxides and scale recovery. DOE steel roadmap chapter 3 §3.1.3 pp.68–70 describes settled coarse scale, sinter use on or off site and oil restrictions. JRC ferrous-processing BREF supports the wet scale-pit co-products. Harsco reports an oily sludge treatment/briquetting counterexample. The sources support a transparent conditional process chain; none certifies a Chinese plant, a shipment, feed status or product grade.",
    "measurement": "The reference is 1 kg actual moist newly released mass, excluding container tare. Independent as-received, dry, iron and oil bases are required. Physical balances use gross flows with wet scale, hot strip, rejects, sludge and real WIP/finished stocks. Allocated burdens follow the source and WIP cohort. Original release/reversal links keep post-release handling and returned skips on the original cohort, with external purchases, first non-purchases and proven returns disjoint.",
    "readiness": "Both languages have 41 atomic exchange cards. Fourteen flow identities were reread from exact native versions; 27 remain unbound, including the finished Product reference and electricity provider. Real legal/receiver transfer status, Chinese mill operations, supplier, chemistry, atmospheric releases and lot records must be supplied. Target check 208 performed, none skipped, 31 quantity warnings. Candidate/authored, Chinese aligned, expert scientific and formal translation reviews pending.",
    "native_records": "Online reads confirm the slab Product, gas Product/Gross calorific value, water Product/Mass, reject, captured dust and oil Waste flows, atmospheric resource oxygen and seven species-specific emissions. Both examined mill-scale records are Waste flows. The Chinese flume-separated record binds the reject only. Neither is the reference Product. Grid consumption uses native Net calorific value; its supplier is not bound to physical Energy/MJ. The archive supplied the Energy group at 03.00.003 while the property cited a historical 01.00.000 target. The meter remains separately documented.",
